I also added local support/shim headers under [_support](/ssd1/zqy/Multi-hdl-language-repo/hls_dataset/function_verify/_support) and minimal local CNN support headers under [03-Headers](/ssd1/zqy/Multi-hdl-language-repo/hls_dataset/function_verify/03-Headers) so the generated benches include the real copied DUTs instead of doing snippet-only checks.

Verification was run with `g++` on all 21 generated DUT benches. Twenty compile checks reached the copied DUT and failed at the literal `<TARGET>` hole inside the DUT source, which confirms the benches are wired to the real candidate files. One extra environment blocker remains for `bubble_sort`: `fast_float.h` needs `ac_fixed.h`, which is not available here. The exact per-folder results and blocker reasons are in [_agent_status.md](/ssd1/zqy/Multi-hdl-language-repo/hls_dataset/function_verify/_agent_status.md).
